<title>USA: Zytec to sell $12 million of debentures.</title>
<headline>Zytec to sell $12 million of debentures.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zytec Corp said Tuesday it arranged for the private sale of $12 million of convertible subordinated debentures.</p>
<p>The debentures, which offer an interest rate of 7.5 percent and mature in 2001, will be convertible into Zytec common stock at $13.68 a share.</p>
<p>In September, Zytec withdrew a registration statement for a public offer of more than 2.2 million common shares, saying it would seek alternative methods of long-term financing.</p>
<p>The company makes power conversion equipment.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787</p>
